  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Waly Fish Farming Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a response to the decline of fishery resources and the problem of unemployment among young people and women in the region. The challenges of the project are multiple: (i) develop a large profitable fish farm in the area; (ii) contribute to the harmonious development of aquaculture in Mauritania; (iii) make up for the decline in sea fishing catches in Mauritania and the shortage of products fisheries in several regions; (iv) contribute to food security by making quality products available to consumers very good quality; (v) reduce youth and female unemployment in the region; (vi) participate in the training of stakeholders in aquaculture; (viii) develop a competitive and environmentally friendly private sector; (ix) label fish products Waly aqua for export.</narrative>
  </description>
